.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OUTPUT
.sp
IsTruncated \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A flag that indicates whether Amazon S3 returned all of the results that satisfied the search criteria. If your results were truncated, you can make a follow\-up paginated request by using the \fBNextKeyMarker\fP and \fBNextVersionIdMarker\fP response parameters as a starting place in another request to return the rest of the results.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
KeyMarker \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Marks the last key returned in a truncated response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
VersionIdMarker \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Marks the last version of the key returned in a truncated response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
NextKeyMarker \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When the number of responses exceeds the value of \fBMaxKeys\fP , \fBNextKeyMarker\fP specifies the first key not returned that satisfies the search criteria. Use this value for the key\-marker request parameter in a subsequent request.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
NextVersionIdMarker \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When the number of responses exceeds the value of \fBMaxKeys\fP , \fBNextVersionIdMarker\fP specifies the first object version not returned that satisfies the search criteria. Use this value for the \fBversion\-id\-marker\fP request parameter in a subsequent request.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Versions \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for version information.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The version of an object.
.sp
ETag \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The entity tag is an MD5 hash of that version of the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumAlgorithm \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The algorithm that was used to create a checksum of the object.
.sp
(string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC32\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC32C\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSHA1\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSHA256\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCRC64NVME\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The checksum type that is used to calculate the object’s checksum value. For more information, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOMPOSITE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFULL_OBJECT\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Size \-> (long)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Size in bytes of the object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
StorageClass \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The class of storage used to store the object.
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSTANDARD\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Key \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The object key.
.sp
Constraints:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
min: \fB1\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
VersionId \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Version ID of an object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
IsLatest \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether the object is (true) or is not (false) the latest version of an object.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
LastModified \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Date and time when the object was last modified.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Owner \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the owner of the object.
.sp
DisplayName \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the display name of the owner. This value is only supported in the following Amazon Web Services Regions:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
US East (N. Virginia)
.IP \(bu 2
US West (N. California)
.IP \(bu 2
US West (Oregon)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Singapore)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Sydney)
.IP \(bu 2
Asia Pacific (Tokyo)
.IP \(bu 2
Europe (Ireland)
.IP \(bu 2
South America (São Paulo)
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ID \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the ID of the owner.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RestoreStatus \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the restoration status of an object. Objects in certain storage classes must be restored before they can be retrieved. For more information about these storage classes and how to work with archived objects, see \fI\%Working with archived objects\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
IsRestoreInProgress \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies whether the object is currently being restored. If the object restoration is in progress, the header returns the value \fBTRUE\fP . For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqtrue\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the object restoration has completed, the header returns the value \fBFALSE\fP . For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqfalse\(dq, RestoreExpiryDate=\(dq2012\-12\-21T00:00:00.000Z\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the object hasn\(aqt been restored, there is no header response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RestoreExpiryDate \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates when the restored copy will expire. This value is populated only if the object has already been restored. For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBx\-amz\-optional\-object\-attributes: IsRestoreInProgress=\(dqfalse\(dq, RestoreExpiryDate=\(dq2012\-12\-21T00:00:00.000Z\(dq\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
DeleteMarkers \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for an object that is a delete marker. To learn more about delete markers, see \fI\%Working with delete markers\fP .
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Information about the delete marker.
.sp
Owner \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The account that created the delete marker.
.sp
DisplayName \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the display name of the owner. This value is only supported in the following Amazon Web Services Regions:
