.sp
LastModified \-> (timestamp)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Date and time when the object was last modified.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Name \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The bucket name.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Selects objects that start with the value supplied by this parameter.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Delimiter \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The delimiter grouping the included keys. A delimiter is a character that you specify to group keys. All keys that contain the same string between the prefix and the first occurrence of the delimiter are grouped under a single result element in \fBCommonPrefixes\fP . These groups are counted as one result against the \fBmax\-keys\fP limitation. These keys are not returned elsewhere in the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
MaxKeys \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Specifies the maximum number of objects to return.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
CommonPrefixes \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
All of the keys rolled up into a common prefix count as a single return when calculating the number of returns.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for all (if there are any) keys between Prefix and the next occurrence of the string specified by a delimiter. CommonPrefixes lists keys that act like subdirectories in the directory specified by Prefix. For example, if the prefix is notes/ and the delimiter is a slash (/) as in notes/summer/july, the common prefix is notes/summer/.
.sp
Prefix \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Container for the specified common prefix.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
EncodingType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Encoding type used by Amazon S3 to encode object key names in the XML response.
.sp
If you specify the \fBencoding\-type\fP request parameter, Amazon S3 includes this element in the response, and returns encoded key name values in the following response elements:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBKeyMarker, NextKeyMarker, Prefix, Key\fP , and \fBDelimiter\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBurl\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
RequestCharged \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
If present, indicates that the requester was successfully charged for the request. For more information, see \fI\%Using Requester Pays buckets for storage transfers and usage\fP in the \fIAmazon Simple Storage Service user guide\fP .
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This functionality is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrequester\fP
